{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ref_child_aliased",
    "description": "A REFERENCED child carrying the deprecated `\"op\": \"aggregate\"` spelling. The alias must be normalized in the CHILD too: normalization happens at one wire boundary per binding, applied to every document a load touches \u2014 root, `{ref}` child, template library, coupling library. Before that was true, the alias (and `arrayop`) survived a `{ref}` all the way into `emit` in Python and Rust, silently, with no warning \u2014 falsifying docs/content/rfcs/faq-node-rename.md \u00a75.2. Every fixture in this suite used to be a single self-contained document, which is exactly why five green binding suites never saw it.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "faq",
      "deprecated_op_alias",
      "ref",
      "conformance"
    ]
  },
